+
+All eight listings are accounted for: four qualify and four are ruled out. One-time pet deposits are disclosed for context but are not added to monthly totals, and optional parking charges are likewise kept outside those totals.
+
+## Recommendation
+
+**Primary recommendation: Alder Court.** Its 31-minute trip is the shortest among homes that meet the corrected October 15 start and every other hard requirement. It also has in-unit laundry and the lowest recurring monthly housing cost among the qualifiers, $2,550, making it the strongest overall fit without overriding the commute-first ranking.
+
+**Backup: Harbor Point.** Harbor is the next-best fit because its 33-minute trip is the second-shortest compliant commute and its $2,600 recurring total includes a parking space. Its chief compromises are shared basement laundry and a third-floor walk-up.
+
+No leasing contact, application, or tour request has been initiated; the current authorization covers this report only.
+
+## Questions to verify before any future action
+
+- Are the quoted unit, base rent, and October 15 start date still available when the user is ready to act?
+- Are any utilities or required monthly charges missing from the supplied fee lists, and can management provide the full lease-fee sheet?
+- Does the cat policy impose breed, age, weight, or number limits beyond the stated deposit and monthly cat rent?
+- How reliable are the scheduled 7:30 a.m. transit times on the user’s actual workdays, especially the one-transfer routes?
+- At Alder, are the in-unit machines maintained by management; at Harbor, how many machines serve the basement laundry room?
